ge moves on Row F. Playing to the edges this early is usually suboptimal as it limits mobility and can give the opponent leverage.\n\nReason: I chose **(F, 3)** because it is the most strategically sound move. It prioritizes piece stability and grouping (mobility) over mere piece count. By playing in the "sweet 16" central square (F3) and flipping enclosed opponent pieces, I deny the opponent easy frontiers and strengthen my control of the board\'s core.\n\nAnswer: (F, 3)'}
